      "hint": "Who is supposed to be doing the checking, you or them?",
      "principle": "You are not the investigator. Nobody expects you to be sure. The people who take tips are trained to ask questions, and they would rather hear something that turns out to be nothing than miss something real. Saying which part you are unsure about is useful, not weak, because it tells them what to check. Asking around first is the one thing that makes it worse. It warns people, and it spreads something that might not be true.",
      "keyPhrase": {
        "quote": "I'm not sure about this part, but here is what I heard.",
        "gloss": "Not being sure is a reason to say more, not less."
